think The CSS background-repeat family had repeat (compose_tiled), no-repeat (place_paint), space (space_paint) but not round -- and round SCALES the tile, a verb no image module owned; a bounded nearest-neighbor scale is both the Lindy floor (every surface resizes: thumbnails, zoom, the 2x sprite) and the crux that unlocks round
think Confirmed no scale/resample verb exists; the README even named `scale` (nearest-neighbor) as a planned Photos Resample path, so this lands the floor it anticipated
obs scale_nearest(allocator, src, dst_w, dst_h) maps each destination index to its source by one pure integer per-axis rule src_index = dx*src_w/dst_w (the classic nearest floor, si strictly < src_extent proven), copying the nearest pixel whole -- no color math, no blend, no codec; single-stranded over qoi buffers, integer only so deterministic
obs Bounds all up front before any allocation: BadScaleDims (zero dim), EmptySource (no extent), ScaleTooLarge (past qoi_max_dim or qoi_max_pixels); all-or-nothing so a refusal allocates nothing
obs Selftest crux proven on metal GREEN first run: identity byte-for-byte, 2x upscale into four clean 2x2 blocks inventing no between-color, 2x downscale sampling nearest cols 0 and 2 (not an average), a non-integer 2->3 map bending so the middle cell repeats col 0, a translucent source carrying its exact alpha byte (nearest carries, never blends), QOI round-trip byte-for-byte, three named refusals allocating nothing, determinism
